{#
  monthly_full -- the full monthly email.

  Same house rules as daily_full and weekly_full: inline styles only, tables for
  layout, no external assets, every list guarded with `or []`, and the report
  LEADS with missed work (MISSED_WORK_MODEL.md section 7).

  WHAT THIS REPORT IS FOR, and how it differs from the other two:

    DAILY   what did we lose yesterday, what needs doing today.
    WEEKLY  what should we change, ranked, each with its number.
    MONTHLY is it working. Trend and strategy, not incident.

  So every section here is a COMPARISON. A bare count belongs in the daily; a
  count next to last month's count, with a direction, is the only thing this
  report is allowed to lead with. Four questions, in order:

    1. Which causes grew and which shrank, month over month.
    2. Which clients are on a trajectory -- gaining, decaying, or gone.
    3. Did the close-offs we asked for actually take effect.
    4. Is the coverage gap closing, hour by hour.

  Question 4 is the one this whole system exists to answer. Verified over 30
  days: Agero offers inside Mon-Fri 06:00-18:00 expired 57 times out of 989
  (5.8%); outside those hours, 627 out of 1,017 (61.7%). Same trucks, same
  staff, near-flawless response when somebody is there. That is a COVERAGE
  problem, and one month against the month before is the evidence a staffing
  decision is actually made on.

  EVERY RANKED LIST IS RANKED BY JOB COUNT. offerAmount is empty on 100% of the
  records this account produces, so there is no dollar figure to show and none
  may be implied.
#}
<div style="font-family:-apple-system,Segoe UI,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:#1c1c1c;max-width:680px;">

  <h2 style="margin:0 0 4px 0;font-size:19px;">Towbook monthly &mdash; {{ month_name }}</h2>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:16px;">
    {{ month_start }} to {{ month_end }} ({{ days_in_month }} days),
    against {{ prior_month_name }} &middot; generated {{ generated_at }}
    &middot; rules {{ rules_version }}
  </div>

  {% if missed_available %}
  {# --------------------------------------------------------------------
     THE HEADLINE, AND IT IS A COMPARISON. Each tile carries this month's
     number and last month's underneath it, because the monthly report has
     no business showing a level without its direction.
  -------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:10px 22px 10px 0;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Missed</div>
        <div style="font-size:30px;font-weight:700;color:#b42318;">{{ missed | num }}</div>
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">
          of {{ missed_offers | num }} offered &middot; {{ missed_pct }}%<br>
          {{ prior_month_label }}: {{ missed_prior | num }}
        </div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding:10px 22px;border-left:1px solid #e3e3e3;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Recoverable</div>
        <div style="font-size:30px;font-weight:700;">{{ recoverable | num }}</div>
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">
          {{ recoverable_pct }}% of offers<br>
          {{ prior_month_label }}: {{ recoverable_prior | num }}
        </div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding:10px 22px;border-left:1px solid #e3e3e3;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Nobody answered</div>
        <div style="font-size:30px;font-weight:700;">{{ no_response | num }}</div>
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">
          {{ no_response_pct }}% of offers<br>
          {{ prior_month_label }}: {{ no_response_prior | num }}
        </div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding:10px 22px;border-left:1px solid #e3e3e3;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Client withdrew</div>
        <div style="font-size:30px;font-weight:700;color:#666;">{{ withdrew | num }}</div>
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">
          reported separately<br>
          {{ prior_month_label }}: {{ withdrew_prior | num }}
        </div>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:18px;">
    {{ ranking_note }}
    Recoverable excludes client withdrawals ({{ recoverable_excluding_withdrew | num }});
    including them it is {{ recoverable_including_withdrew | num }}.
    {# Truthiness, not `is not none`: a missing key is Undefined, which IS not
       none and would print "None offers/day". A zero-offer month legitimately
       has nothing to compare and drops the sentence. #}
    {% if offers_per_day and prior_offers_per_day %}
    Months are different lengths, so volume is also stated per day:
    <strong>{{ offers_per_day }} offers/day</strong> this month against
    {{ prior_offers_per_day }} last.
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if narrative %}
  <div style="background:#f6f7f9;border-left:3px solid #2f6feb;padding:12px 14px;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div style="font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;color:#666;margin-bottom:6px;">
      Analyst{% if llm and llm != 'anthropic' %} ({{ llm }}){% endif %}
    </div>
    <div>{{ narrative }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if missed_trend_causes %}
  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
     QUESTION 1. Direction per cause, with both numbers. `direction` arrives
     from metrics.py already decided (up / down / flat / new / gone), so the
     template never has to work out what a negative delta means.
  --------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 4px 0;">Which causes grew, and which shrank</h3>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    {{ month_name }} against {{ prior_month_name }}. {{ ranking_note }}
  </div>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Cause</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Direction</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">This month</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Last month</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Change</th>
    </tr>
    {% for row in missed_trend_causes or [] %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.cause }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
        {% if row.direction == 'up' %}<span style="color:#b42318;font-weight:600;">growing</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'down' %}<span style="color:#137333;font-weight:600;">shrinking</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'new' %}<span style="color:#b42318;font-weight:600;">new</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'gone' %}<span style="color:#137333;font-weight:600;">gone</span>
        {% else %}<span style="color:#666;">flat</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;font-weight:600;">{{ row.missed | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.missed_prior | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
        {# `row.delta and ... > 0` rather than `is not none`: an absent key is
           Undefined, which is falsy but explodes on a comparison. #}
        {% if row.delta and row.delta > 0 %}+{% endif %}{{ row.delta }}
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if coverage_trend %}
  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
     QUESTION 4, AND THE MOST IMPORTANT TABLE IN THIS EMAIL.

     Hour of day, this month against last, in unanswered rate. Only hours
     that saw offers in either month are shown -- a row of zeros for 04:00
     on a month with no 04:00 traffic is noise pretending to be evidence.

     NEGATIVE movement is good: fewer offers going unanswered.
  --------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 4px 0;">Coverage &mdash; is the gap closing?</h3>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    Share of offers nobody answered, by hour of day, {{ month_name }} against
    {{ prior_month_name }}. The median response window Towbook allows is
    3 minutes, so an unanswered offer is a lost job almost immediately.
    A <strong>negative</strong> change is an improvement.
  </div>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Hour</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Offers</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Unanswered</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">This month</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Last month</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Change</th>
    </tr>
    {% for row in coverage_trend or [] %}
    {% if row.offers or row.offers_prior %}
    <tr{% if row.is_blind_spot %} style="background:#fff4f2;"{% endif %}>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
        {{ row.label }}{% if row.is_blind_spot %} <span style="color:#b42318;font-size:11px;">blind spot</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.offers | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;font-weight:600;">{{ row.no_response | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.no_response_rate | pct }}%</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#666;">{{ row.no_response_rate_prior | pct }}%</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
        {% if row.direction == 'better' %}<span style="color:#137333;font-weight:600;">{{ row.delta_pp }}</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'worse' %}<span style="color:#b42318;font-weight:600;">+{{ row.delta_pp }}</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'flat' %}<span style="color:#666;">flat</span>
        {% else %}<span style="color:#999;">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if missed_trend %}
  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
     QUESTION 3. Did what we asked for last month actually happen?

     `.get(...)` all the way down, not attribute chaining: Jinja's Undefined
     raises on a second attribute access, and this whole block would then be
     swallowed by the renderer's fallback rather than rendering what it can.
  --------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  {% set missed_pair = missed_trend.get('totals', {}).get('missed', {}) %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;">Did last month's actions take effect?</h3>
  <ul style="margin:0 0 20px 0;padding-left:20px;">
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      Missed {{ missed_pair.get('missed') | num }} this month against
      {{ missed_pair.get('missed_prior') | num }} last
      &mdash; <strong>{{ missed_pair.get('direction', 'flat') }}</strong>.
      Miss rate moved {{ missed_trend.missed_rate_pp }} points.
    </li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      Unanswered rate moved {{ missed_trend.no_response_rate_pp }} points;
      acceptance moved {{ missed_trend.acceptance_rate_pp }} points.
    </li>
    {% if (missed_trend.closeoff_candidates or {}).resolved %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      No longer being offered &mdash; <strong>a close-off that worked</strong>:
      {{ ((missed_trend.closeoff_candidates or {}).resolved or []) | join(', ') }}.
    </li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if (missed_trend.closeoff_candidates or {}).persisting %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      Still being offered after a second month &mdash; the ask did not land:
      {{ ((missed_trend.closeoff_candidates or {}).persisting or []) | join(', ') }}.
    </li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if (missed_trend.closeoff_candidates or {}).new %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      New close-off candidates:
      {{ ((missed_trend.closeoff_candidates or {}).new or []) | join(', ') }}.
    </li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if (missed_trend.blind_spots or {}).closed %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      Blind spots <strong>closed</strong>:
      {{ ((missed_trend.blind_spots or {}).closed or []) | join(', ') }}.
    </li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if (missed_trend.blind_spots or {}).opened %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      Blind spots <strong>opened</strong>:
      {{ ((missed_trend.blind_spots or {}).opened or []) | join(', ') }}.
    </li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if (missed_trend.blind_spots or {}).persisting %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      Still unmanned after a second month:
      {{ ((missed_trend.blind_spots or {}).persisting or []) | join(', ') }}.
    </li>
    {% endif %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}

  {% if client_trend %}
  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
     QUESTION 2. Client trajectories. Volume AND rate, both months, because
     a client sending less work and a client we accept less of are two
     different problems with two different conversations.
  --------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 4px 0;">Client trajectories</h3>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    {{ month_name }} against {{ prior_month_name }}. {{ ranking_note }}
  </div>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Client</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Offers</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Last month</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Volume</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Acceptance</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Move</th>
    </tr>
    {% for row in client_trend or [] %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.client }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;font-weight:600;">{{ row.offers | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#666;">{{ row.offers_prior | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
        {% if row.volume_delta and row.volume_delta > 0 %}+{% endif %}{{ row.volume_delta }}
      </td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.accepted | pct(row.offers) }}%</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
        {% if row.direction == 'up' %}<span style="color:#137333;font-weight:600;">up {{ row.delta_pp }}</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'down' %}<span style="color:#b42318;font-weight:600;">down {{ row.delta_pp }}</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'new' %}<span style="color:#666;">new</span>
        {% elif row.direction == 'lost' %}<span style="color:#b42318;font-weight:600;">gone</span>
        {% else %}<span style="color:#666;">flat</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if weekly_distribution %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 4px 0;">Within the month</h3>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    Week by week, so a month that improved and a month that decayed do not read
    the same. Partial weeks at either end are marked.
  </div>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Week</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Offered</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Accepted</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Rate</th>
    </tr>
    {% for row in weekly_distribution or [] %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
        {{ row.first_day }} to {{ row.last_day }}{% if row.partial %}
        <span style="color:#888;font-size:11px;">({{ row.days }}d)</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.offered | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.accepted | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.accepted | pct(row.offered) }}%</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if missed_inventory %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 4px 0;">What we did not get</h3>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    Work the acceptance policy says we want, grouped by cause.
    <strong>{{ ranking_note }}</strong>
  </div>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Work</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Cause</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Missed</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Of all missed</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Recoverable</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">What it takes</th>
    </tr>
    {% for row in missed_inventory or [] %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.service_class }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.cause }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;font-weight:600;">{{ row.missed | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.missed_share | pct }}%</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.recoverable | num }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#444;">
        <strong>{{ row.remedy }}</strong>{% if row.question %} &mdash; {{ row.question }}{% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% if missed_inventory_meta and missed_inventory_meta.missed_in_window %}
  <div style="color:#888;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:20px;">
    {{ missed_inventory_meta.missed_in_inventory | num }} of
    {{ missed_inventory_meta.missed_in_window | num }} missed offers are in this table;
    the rest are service classes outside the acceptance policy.
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  {# Which jobs, by the reference Towbook searches on. A month misses far more
     than the list shows, so it caps and says so; the dashboard has them all. #}
  {% include "_missed_jobs.html.j2" %}

  {% if closeoff_clients %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 4px 0;">Work to close off &mdash; ask these clients to stop</h3>
  <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    {% if closeoff_rationale %}{{ closeoff_rationale }}{% endif %} {{ ranking_note }}
  </div>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Client</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Service type</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Offers</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Accepted</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Of their offers</th>
    </tr>
    {% for client in closeoff_clients or [] %}
      {% for row in client.service_types or [] %}
      <tr>
        <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{% if loop.first %}{{ client.client }}{% endif %}</td>
        <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.service_type_raw }}</td>
        <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.offers | num }}</td>
        <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.accepted | num }}</td>
        <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.share_of_client_offers | pct }}%</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if client_gap_findings %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;">Clients that should behave alike, and do not</h3>
  {% for finding in client_gap_findings or [] %}
  <div style="background:#fff4f2;border-left:3px solid #b42318;padding:10px 12px;margin-bottom:10px;">
    <div style="font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;color:#666;">
      {{ finding.kind }} &middot; ranked by {{ finding.ranked_by }} &middot; {{ finding.spread_pp }} points apart
    </div>
    <div>{{ finding.summary }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if trend_statements %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;">What changed versus last month</h3>
  <ul style="margin:0 0 20px 0;padding-left:20px;">
    {% for item in trend_statements or [] %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      {{ item.statement }}
      <span style="color:#666;">({{ item.supporting_number }})</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}

  {% if cause_assessments %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;">What to do next month</h3>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Cause</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Want it?</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">What it would take</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Numbers</th>
    </tr>
    {% for item in cause_assessments or [] %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ item.cause }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ item.want_this_work }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ item.what_it_would_take }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#666;">{{ item.supporting_number }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if close_off_requests %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;">Asks for the clients</h3>
  <ul style="margin:0 0 20px 0;padding-left:20px;">
    {% for item in close_off_requests or [] %}
    <li style="margin-bottom:5px;">
      Ask <strong>{{ item.client }}</strong> to stop sending {{ item.service_type }}
      <span style="color:#666;">({{ item.supporting_number }})</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}

  {% if clients_needing_attention %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;">Clients needing attention</h3>
  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Client</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Reason</th>
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Numbers</th>
    </tr>
    {% for item in clients_needing_attention or [] %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ item.client }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ item.reason }}</td>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#666;">{{ item.supporting_numbers }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
     SUPPORTING CONTEXT. Acceptance rate is a symptom; it is reported after
     the trend, not instead of it.
  --------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:22px 0 8px 0;border-top:1px solid #e3e3e3;padding-top:16px;">
    Supporting context &mdash; what we did accept
  </h3>

  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-bottom:16px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 20px 6px 0;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Offered</div>
        <div style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;">{{ offered | num }}</div>
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">{{ prior_month_label }}: {{ prior_offered | num }}</div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding:6px 20px;border-left:1px solid #e3e3e3;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Accepted</div>
        <div style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;">{{ accepted | num }}</div>
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">{{ prior_month_label }}: {{ prior_accepted | num }}</div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding:6px 20px;border-left:1px solid #e3e3e3;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Acceptance</div>
        <div style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;">{{ rate_pct }}%</div>
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">{{ prior_month_label }}: {{ prior_rate_pct }}%</div>
      </td>
      <td style="padding:6px 20px;border-left:1px solid #e3e3e3;">
        <div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;">Denied</div>
        <div style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;">{{ denied | num }}</div>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Service class</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Offered</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Accepted</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Rate</th>
    </tr>
    {% for name, stats in (service_classes or {}).items() %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ name }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ stats.offered | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ stats.accepted | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ stats.accepted | pct(stats.offered) }}%</td>
    </tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="4" style="padding:6px 8px;color:#666;">No service class breakdown in this window.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>

  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
         style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:13px;">
    <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
      <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Client</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Offered</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Accepted</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Denied</th>
      <th align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Rate</th>
    </tr>
    {% for row in clients or [] %}
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.client_name or row.client_key }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.offered | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.accepted | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.denied | num }}</td>
      <td align="right" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.accepted | pct(row.offered) }}%</td>
    </tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="5" style="padding:6px 8px;color:#666;">No per-client rows in this window.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>

  {% if proposed_rules %}
  <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 8px 0;">Proposed rule changes ({{ (proposed_rules or []) | length }})</h3>
  <div style="background:#fff8e6;border:1px solid #f0d9a0;padding:12px 14px;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div style="margin-bottom:8px;">
      Written to <code>config/rules.proposed.yaml</code> for review. They have
      <strong>no effect</strong> on classification, metrics, alerting or notification
      until a human copies the fragment into <code>config/rules.yaml</code>.
    </div>
    {% for item in proposed_rules or [] %}
    <div style="margin-bottom:12px;">
      <div><strong>{{ item.id }}</strong>
        {% if item.occurrence_count %}<span style="color:#666;">&middot; {{ item.occurrence_count }} requests since {{ item.first_seen }}</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div style="margin:3px 0;">{{ item.rationale }}</div>
      {% if item.service_type_raw_samples %}
      <div style="color:#666;font-size:12px;">
        Saw: {% for sample in item.service_type_raw_samples or [] %}<code>{{ sample }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div style="color:#888;font-size:11px;border-top:1px solid #e3e3e3;padding-top:10px;">
    Towbook Job Acceptance Intelligence &middot; report {{ report_type }} &middot; times are local
    ({{ generated_at }}). The rules that produced these numbers are version {{ rules_version }}.
    <strong>{{ ranking_note }}</strong>
    {# WHY THESE TOTALS ARE LOWER THAN THE PORTAL'S. A club that gets no answer
       asks again; the repeat is the same job and is counted once. Stated on
       every report, because an owner reconciling a total against Towbook and
       finding it short is owed the reason without having to ask. #}
    {% if duplicates_note %}<br><strong>{{ duplicates_note }}</strong>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
